  # recovered from reports/batch_20260918T105936Z/F07/inputs/case.yaml
  F07:
    title: the adapter of a robot on its way to pickup dies
    runners:
    - r01
    scenario: f_fault_triggers
    submit:
    - cargo: f07-cargo
      drop: S_right_b
      pick: S_left_a
      request_id: f07-run
    steps:
    - do:
        action: kill_process
        node: nav2_adapter
        runner: r01
      when:
        request_id: f07-run
        state: EXECUTING
    observe_s: 900.0
    truth: fleet_recorder
    expect:
      behavior: PASS
      safety: PASS
      task: NEEDS_ATTENTION
    note: 'Section 6: Adapter 退出只终止该 run 目标进程，Gate 保持运行. That is why the target is `nav2_adapter` and not
      `all`: the gate, the bridge and Nav2 keep running, and it is the TASK LAYER that has to notice the
      robot has gone quiet and park the run. What ends the leg is the state going stale, not a timeout --
      `f_fault_triggers` sets `leg_timeout_s: 120` and the freshness window is much shorter than that, so
      a park inside the budget is the adapter''s death being noticed rather than the budget expiring.

      '
